k appears to execute but no dialog/form appears for entering template name/description. No input elements, dialogs, or status notifications found after clicking Save Current.\", \"evidence\": \"Save Current button exists with action 'save-as-template'. Click registered but no dialog, modal, input field, or confirmation toast appeared. No dialog or input elements found in DOM after click.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Successfully switched between all three scenarios: Recruitment→Training→Promotion. simulation.active-scenario updated each time (Recruitment Simulation, Training Simulation, Promotion Simulation). Training scenario showed different default adjustments (Technical: +1, Domain: +1) compared to Recruitment (all 0). Scenario descriptions and category adjustments updated with each switch.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Simulation results not observable after running. Run Simulation button clicked but metrics remain unchanged after execution (Coverage: 78%, Avg Level: 3.8, Critical Path: 4, Gaps: 0 before and after). Promotion scenario adjustments (Technical -5%, Behavioral +10%, Leadership +20%) do not appear to affect displayed outputs.\", \"actual\": \"All metrics unchanged after clicking Run Simulation. Coverage 78%→78%, Avg Level 3.8→3.8, Critical Path 4→4, Gaps 0→0. No visual indication of simulation results in model outputs.\", \"evidence\": \"Run Simulation button exists and click registered. Promotion scenario shows weight adjustments for 4 categories. Metrics displayed but did not change after simulation execution.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Unable to interact with competency level buttons due to React Flow node event interception. Attempted click on set-level-3 button timed out with Collaboration node and header intercepting pointer events. Cannot complete test of model state persistence.\", \"actual\": \"Click timeout when attempting to set competency level. Other page elements (header, other competency nodes) intercepted pointer events, preventing reliable interaction with level buttons.\", \"evidence\": \"Error: browserBackend timeout 5000ms. Element located but multiple retries failed due to pointer event interception from sibling/parent elements in React Flow graph.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All observable competency levels (Advanced 5, Intermediate 3) and weights (90%, 80%, 60%, 90%, 70%, 50%) conform to specified ranges. Levels display values representing 1-5 range. Weights all display as percentages within 10%-100% range. No values observed outside constraints. Simulation scenario weight adjustments are relative (-5%, +10%, +20%, 0%) applied to absolute weights.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Coverage percentage updated in real-time following interactions: after clicking toggles/weight controls, coverage changed from 68%→67%→69% without page reload. Critical path also updated in real-time: 3→5→3. Metrics display without requiring page reload or explicit save action. Progress indicators update as soon as interactions complete.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All three simulation scenarios are fully initialized with default adjustments visible: Recruitment (Technical: -1 level/0% weight, Behavioral: 0 level/+10% weight, Leadership: -2 level/-10% weight, Domain: -1 level/0% weight), Training (Technical: +1 level, Behavioral: 0, Leadership: 0, Domain: +1), Promotion (Technical: -5% weight, Behavioral: +10%, Leadership: +20%). Adjustments displayed immediately upon scenario selection without requiring prior interaction.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph controls display current competency values in real-time: all competencies show current levels (Advanced/Intermediate) and weights (90%, 80%, 60%, 90%, 70%, 50%). Critical path count (4) and gaps count (0) are observable and consistent. Metrics display (coverage 78%, avg-level 3.8, critical-path 4, gaps 0) align with graph state. Earlier interactions showed metrics updated immediately (coverage 68%→67%→69%, critical-path 3→5→3) demonstrating real-time synchronization between graph state and metrics summary.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph displays as interactive directed weighted graph with: 6 competency nodes (Programming Languages Advanced 90%, System Design Intermediate 80%, Code Review Intermediate 60%, Problem Solving Advanced 90%, Collaboration Intermediate 70%, Agile Methodology Intermediate 50%), relationship edges with visible weights, and graph controls (zoom in/out, fit view). Nodes are draggable (FT-3 confirmed) and visible in React Flow canvas.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Critical path recalculates and updates after model changes. When Software Engineer template was active: critical path count 3 (with Programming Languages, Problem Solving, System Design). When Product Manager template applied: critical path count changed to 4. Metric updates immediately upon template application. All competencies in current view are enabled (enabled: true for all 6), valid path through enabled competencies confirmed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Unable to create risk-gap scenario to test. High-weight competency level buttons not reliably clickable due to React Flow node event interception. Current model shows 0 gaps but cannot lower competency levels to create risk-gap condition for testing.\", \"actual\": \"Level adjustment buttons timeout and fail to respond. Gap count remains 0. Unable to confirm risk-gap